MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Corazon feels like a natural next choice because Santana's guitar-driven music connects with the Clapton and Hendrix albums in my recent listening; it is the one I would try today.",
    "The later Beatles material fits my classic rock interests, and Norah Jones could suit quieter listening, even though neither makes me want to choose another album today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "A broad 80s compilation and Patsy Cline's traditional country vocals miss the blues and roots-rock direction that interests me right now.",
    "Wallflower feels less suited to my current interest in rock guitar, while Greatest Hits and Definitive Collection give me no identifiable artist connection to judge whether I would enjoy them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to assume that an interest in established rock musicians means I want broad collections of familiar older music.",
    "Some choices stretch my interest in roots-oriented music into softer vocals or traditional country, although those sounds are not interchangeable for me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The guitar playing and blues influence connecting my Clapton and Hendrix listening matter more to me than a shared era.",
    "My recent choices include individual albums by established musicians, so another distinctive album can feel more relevant than a greatest-hits collection; a loose connection is rarely enough for me to act."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in established rock artists but only partly capture the blues-influenced guitar sound that would make me choose something today."
}
